    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d846">

                <pb facs="1141" n="1005" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg1005"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">196.6/1094</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Netherlands Legation to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1776</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Note Verbale</hi></p>
                <p>The Netherland Legation has noticed that a bill (S. 314) has been introduced by
                    Senator LaFollette relating to the payment of advance wages and allotments in
                    respect to seamen on foreign vessels and making further provision for carrying
                    out the purpose of the Seamen’s Act, approved March 4, 1915,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d846-f1"/> which bill is a copy of the bill introduced during last
                    session by the same Senator and passed by the Senate on April 24, 1928.</p>
                <p>The Royal Legation has the honor to inform the State Department that the remarks
                    made on behalf of the Netherland Government by its note of May 3, 1928, No.
                        1413,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d846-f2"/> are in the same way applicable to the
                    new bill.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1929-05-15">May 15,
                            1929</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
